{"created": "2026-09-24T02:39:34.823509+00:00", "modified": "2026-09-24T02:39:35.197237+00:00", "id": 22928337, "conceptrecid": "22928336", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22928337", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22928336", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22928337", "metadata": {"title": "New lower bounds for the degree-diameter problem from Cayley graphs, orbit graphs and lifts", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22928337", "publication_date": "2026-09-24", "description": "<p>We give 21 new lower bounds for the degree-diameter problem with degree d &le; 20 and&nbsp;diameter k &le; 10. Of the graphs, 15 are Cayley graphs of semidirect products of two cyclic&nbsp;groups with explicit generating sets, the largest having 2,007,474 vertices at degree 12 and&nbsp;diameter 7. Three are orbit graphs of finite groups acting with three vertex orbits: on 252&nbsp;vertices from A7 at (d, k) = (5, 4), on 441 vertices from PSU(3, 3) at (6, 4) and on 119 vertices&nbsp;from PGL(2, 7) at (6, 3). One is a bi-Cayley graph on 216 vertices at (16, 2), obtained from a&nbsp;sufficient condition for diameter two. The other two are affine line lifts, on 35,328 vertices at&nbsp;(20, 4) and on 197,316 vertices at (18, 5). Every graph is given explicitly, in the paper or in&nbsp;the accompanying dataset, and its degree and diameter are verified by breadth-first search.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Rajiv, Rishabh", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0009-0000-8626-5234"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22928336"}}]}}, "title": "New lower bounds for the degree-diameter problem from Cayley graphs, orbit graphs and lifts", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22928337", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22928337", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22928337?preview=1", "